Attribution — source work this repository adapts (not copied verbatim):

- Source repository: andyhuo520/vibe-knowledge
  https://github.com/andyhuo520/vibe-knowledge
- Source license: MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Berryxia (andyhuo520)
- What was adapted: the workflow idea — one knowledge point → one narrated,
  fully sourced code-rendered short video; the six script templates;
  the facts-list rule (every number, name, year and quotation must carry
  a source). The core files listed in README.md ("复制清单") were copied
  from the source on 2026-11-24 after the user confirmed in plain words,
  after seeing the execution-risk warning, and were redacted: the paid
  enhancement tier, the default AI voice, and the forced default BGM were
  removed; the default was changed to vertical 1080x1920 with the user's
  own voice. The scripts in scripts/ and the film skeleton in
  skills/vibe-knowledge/templates/film_skeleton_vertical.html were
  written from scratch for this repository.
- What was NOT copied: the paid-tier tools and references, the remaining
  40 styles, the default BGM and default voice assets, the sample videos,
  and the cine rendering engine (see SOURCE.md).
